CHAPTER 2: CHARACTERISTICS OF THE POPULATION
2.1 Socio-cultural characteristics of the population
2.1.1 Nationality of the population of Kicukiro district
The results of the 5th Rwanda Population and Housing Census (RPHC) conducted in
2022 reveal that the Rwandan population represents 99.11% at the national level,
while foreigners make up 0.89% of the total population. In the City of Kigali,
foreigners accou nt for 1.18% of the population, and in Kicukiro district, the
percentage of foreigners represent 1.37%, which corresponds to 6,749 foreign
residents. Among the sectors in Kicukiro district, four  sectors have the highest
percentage of foreigners compared to  other sectors. Niboye sector has proportion
of foreigners at 2.81%, followed by Kigarama with 2.57%, Kicukiro with 2.26%, and
Gikondo with 2.08%.
The table below provides a clear illustration of the distribution of the population by
nationality in their respective sectors of residence, showing the percentage of
foreigners in each sector.
